{
  "name": "read-swc-writes-joined-to-readers",
  "description": "A join (`join`): every data element a runnable writes, joined to the connector that carries it and to every runnable that reads it at the other end — the sender-receiver connection table as ONE request. The outer read is a member path with a computed value (`members: \"runnables.writes\"`, `derived: [\"base_type\"]`); the first entry joins each write to the connectors whose computed `connection_ends` provider is the writing component and port, and nests the match under `connection`; the second reaches into that alias with its `left` paths and joins the reads of the requester component and port of the same data element, nested under `reader`. It is an INNER join on equal values: a row with no match is dropped, and a row with several is repeated once per match. Every path is checked against the declared shape of the row it reads before any row is computed.",
  "kind": "example",
  "context": {
    "summary": "The seed of `examples/read-swc-members-path-runnable-writes.json`: the provider writes `pOut.value` in `ExampleRun` and `pPhysical.speed` in both `ExampleRun` and `ExampleSlowRun`; the consumer, one composition level below the root behind two delegated boundary ports, reads both in `ExampleConsumerRun`. So three writes each meet exactly one connector and one read.",
