    "notes": "Each row is the outer identity row, then each match under its alias: the provider component, port and element are `element` and `member`, the writing runnable `through.0`, the implementation and base type `derived.base_type`, the requester `connection.derived.connection_ends.requester`, the reading runnable `reader.through.0`. The joined reads are answered whole and unmeasured; only this answer is measured. Identical rows collapse, and a page's `next` is the whole row, every alias included. A path naming no value of its row is `schema-violation` (`negative/schema-violation-join-path-outside-row.json`), and so is `join` without an explicit `form: \"index\"` (`negative/schema-violation-join-without-index-form.json`)."
